---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL; // e.g. "/emoria/"
---

<Base lang="en" title="About us — EMORIA" current="About us"
  description="EMORIA was founded by Cemil Can Özkaya, a state-certified educator with around ten years of experience in early-years practice.">
  <article class="bg-[var(--color-cream)]">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pb-14 pt-36 text-center">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-[var(--color-brand)]">✦ About us</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl sm:text-6xl">About us</h1>
    </div>

    <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl space-y-6 px-6 pb-20 text-lg text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]">
      <p>
        EMORIA was founded by <strong class="text-[var(--color-ink)]">Cemil Can Özkaya</strong>,
        a state-certified educator with around ten years of experience in integration
        kindergartens, special-needs schools, youth welfare organisations and family counselling.
      </p>
      <p>
        The beginning goes back further than you'd expect. Already in 2020, during his training,
        a first, simple version of this game came together in a Berlin kindergarten: a feeling
        wheel, a few cards, six preschoolers around a table. At the end of the forty minutes, the
        children were asked whether they'd like to do it again. The answer was a unanimous yes.
      </p>
      <p>
        Over the years, that afternoon grew into a complete educational system, refined through
        every further experience in practice, through feedback from professionals, and above all
        through the children themselves.
      </p>
      <p>
        Today, EMORIA is a young company with a clear goal: to give children a language for their
        feelings, and to give the people who work with them every day a tool that truly fits into
        their daily routine.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-[var(--color-cream-deep)]">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl space-y-6 px-6 py-20 text-lg text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]">
        <h2 class="text-center text-3xl text-[var(--color-ink)]">About EMORIA</h2>
        <p>
          Children learn to count. Children learn to read. Children learn to tie their shoes.
        </p>
        <p class="italic text-[var(--color-ink)]">
          But who teaches them to talk about their feelings?
        </p>
        <p>
          Emotional education is part of every education programme today. What's often missing
          in practice is the right tool for it. Educators rarely have the time to develop their
          own material for every conversation about feelings, and many existing offerings never
          go beyond a few cards or posters.
        </p>
        <p>
          EMORIA develops research-based educational tools that address exactly this. Our first
          product, Yubuu's Feeling Wheel, guides children aged four to ten through a clear
          process: from first noticing a feeling, through talking about it, to the question of
          what need actually lies behind it.
        </p>
        <p>
          At the centre is Yubuu, a curious being with no fixed gender and no fixed origin, born
          on the small planet Lumora. Yubuu travels through different worlds to understand how
          differently living beings feel. Yubuu doesn't judge, doesn't hand out correct answers,
          but asks, wonders and listens. That's exactly what makes it easy for children to open up.
        </p>
        <p>
          Yubuu's Feeling Wheel is just the beginning. EMORIA is designed as a growing universe,
          from which more games, materials and stories will emerge over time.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl space-y-6 px-6 py-20 text-lg text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]">
      <p>
        EMORIA is a young company from Berlin that develops educational tools for emotional
        education.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our starting point is an observation from daily work with children: most conflicts don't
        come from bad intentions, but simply because children lack the words to say what's going
        on inside them. And educators, in their full daily routine, often lack the right material
        to change exactly that.
      </p>
      <p>
        Everything created at EMORIA therefore comes from practice, not from a desk. Every
        component has been tested with children over years, discussed with professionals and
        revised again and again until it works in real everyday life.
      </p>
      <p>
        We believe emotional competence should be nurtured just as naturally as language or
        maths. And that good educational materials should take work off professionals' hands,
        not add to it.
      </p>
      <p class="text-center italic text-[var(--color-ink)]">That's exactly what we're working on.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-20 text-center">
      <img src={`${base}img/yubuu-rocket.png`} alt="Yubuu" class="mx-auto mb-4 h-28 w-auto drop-shadow-[0_14px_20px_rgba(43,42,40,0.16)]" />
      <h2 class="text-3xl">Bring EMORIA to your Kita</h2>
      <p class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-lg text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]">
        If your kindergarten or practice would like to be among the first to try EMORIA,
        Cemil would be glad to talk.
      </p>
      <a href={`${base}en/contact`} class="mt-7 inline-block rounded-[var(--radius-pill)] bg-[var(--color-brand)] px-8 py-3.5 font-[var(--font-body)] font-semibold text-white shadow-[var(--shadow-soft)] transition hover:bg-[var(--color-brand-deep)]">
        Get in touch
      </a>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
